From 09aedda61ec1a25f7915606c8cd60e5f39a16bc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 11:02:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] conversation cache: a request that starts with a shallow
 checkpoint of a parked conversation borrows it, the image goes back to its
 place (opt-in STRATA_PARK_BORROW=1, #1164)

A sibling subagent sharing only the main agent's system prompt and tool list (the 8192-token root) took the main
agent's parked 132k image: take() moved it into the session, the subagent's request rewrote every cell past 8192,
and the main agent's next turn read its history again (production log rel 2001/2603/4060: a ping-pong between two
agent families, each restoring "8192 tokens (checkpoint)").

With STRATA_PARK_BORROW=1 such a match borrows instead (conversation_borrow_rule): not the live end, shallower than
the entry's deepest checkpoint (upstream c9e571e0), less than half of the entry (2 * match < its length: a turn that
re-renders a few dozen tokens before the end still takes, so no stale copy stays behind each main-agent turn), and
no pinned shared prefix at or below the match (upstream 2b296987).  Everything else is taken as before.

Unlike upstream (gated on stages.empty(), restore_prefix), the image is still take()n - the outgoing park counts it
as held and cannot evict or supersede it - and restored whole on the validated path (layer split, draftless slot
images, the K/V growth), then the borrower copies only the checkpoints at or below its resume point, stage parts
index-aligned (conversation_borrow_checkpoints), skips retain() and drops the retained K/V, and put_back() returns
the image to its LRU place (park_serial): an entry parked meanwhile that supersedes it drops it, the slot count and
budget evict oldest first, which may be the donor itself.  The SSD tier (its load consumes the file) and a read that
gave way (STRATA_READ_YIELD) never borrow.

Logs "conversation cache: borrowed N of a parked M-token conversation (checkpoint) in X ms; parked=.. bytes=..
checkpoints=.."; with the switch on the "restored" line also names the donor's length ("restored N of M tokens").
Off: nothing changes (put() records park_serial, which nothing else reads).

conversation_cache_test: the rule (incl. the production 8192 / 132245 of 132362 cases), put_back's LRU place,
accounting, slot count, budget, supersede and pinned-only cases, and the checkpoint copy with and without a layer
split (4850 checks).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
